    "text": "\n* (a) The function takes a list of intervals and merges overlapping intervals into a single interval.\n* (b) Time complexity: O(n log n), where n is the number of intervals, due to the sorting step. Space complexity: O(n), as we need to store the sorted intervals in memory.\n* (c) One correctness bug: If two intervals overlap but have different values, only one value will be preserved in the merged interval. For example, if we merge [(1, 3), (2, 4)] into [(1, 4)], we lose the fact that the original intervals had different values.\n* (d) One performance improvement: Instead of sorting the entire list of intervals each time, we can use a binary search to find the insertion point for each new interval. This reduces the time complexity from O(n log n) to O(log n).",
